      <memberdef kind="function" id="os_2posix_2src_2ebf__core_8c_1a7fc8f5b888fff4b4266b71a29f2df517" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="ebf_8h_1a2deeba857b1640697bd4abbb79571010" kindref="member">EBF_WEAK</ref> void</type>
        <definition>EBF_WEAK void EBF_setStdinListener</definition>
        <argsstring>(EBF_stdin_t listener)</argsstring>
        <name>EBF_setStdinListener</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ebf_8h_1ae5791af1ebceacc30e9a8e993eb3df3a" kindref="member">EBF_stdin_t</ref></type>
          <declname>listener</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Registers a callback to receive standard input data. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Defined as weak by default, allowing a custom implementation to override it.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Depending on the stdin implementation, the listener may be called from an ISR context when input data is received. If so, the listener implementation shall be treated as ISR code.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">listener</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Function to be called with incoming data. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="sw/ecf/embedded_base_framework/src/core/os/posix/src/ebf_core.c" line="87" column="15" bodyfile="sw/ecf/embedded_base_framework/src/core/os/posix/src/ebf_core.c" bodystart="87" bodyend="90"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="os_2posix_2src_2ebf__core_8c_1a5b99acb3d2b82895a10f4a113638560f" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="ebf_8h_1a2deeba857b1640697bd4abbb79571010" kindref="member">EBF_WEAK</ref> bool</type>
        <definition>EBF_WEAK bool EBF_stdoutWrite</definition>
        <argsstring>(const uint8_t *data, uint16_t len)</argsstring>
        <name>EBF_stdoutWrite</name>
        <param>
          <type>const uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>data</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint16_t</type>
          <declname>len</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Sends data to the standard output. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Defined as weak by default, allowing a custom implementation to override it.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Since standard output may be a shared resource, all implementations shall be protected using <ref refid="ebf_8h_1a058a9071df8f3bcedc4fff0a9e06ee84" kindref="member">EBF_CRITICAL_SECTION_ENTRY()</ref> and <ref refid="ebf_8h_1ae34944c46809734fbb6dd706bc6779fa" kindref="member">EBF_CRITICAL_SECTION_EXIT()</ref>. Therefore, Calling <ref refid="ebf_8h_1a2270e3785e19164c7cb1974c10a496eb" kindref="member">EBF_stdoutWrite()</ref> from an active EBF critical section violates the contract, as nested critical sections are not supported.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Supported message length is implementation dependent.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>A false return value indicates that the data cannot be serialized and shall be handled explicitly by the caller, preferably using EAF asserts. Silently discarding the data is highly discouraged.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to data to be sent. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">len</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Length of the data in bytes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>true if all data was accepted for transmission; false otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
